1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:24,923
The duke sent flowers after his men shot up my room. Three hundred
blue roses. The card said he deplored the recent unpleasantness and
hoped we would attend his masquerade aboard the Sovereign Sun. Tank
read it twice, then held it at arm's length. Nigga deplores.
Apparently. Say it again. Deplores. Nah, nigga. In his voice. I raised
my chin.

2
00:00:25,173 --> 00:00:49,727
I deplore that my niggas missed. Tank bent over the flowers. Shawna
took the card before he could wipe his eyes with it. Evidence, she
said. Evidence this nigga need to hire a poet. Or better men, I said.
Don't help him. Porsche counted the arrangements from the doorway.
Three hundred roses. No apology to the hotel. No money for the workers
who cleaned up.

3
00:00:49,977 --> 00:01:10,571
Nigga thinks stems are currency. Mercedes pulled a vase toward her. We
can send these to the staff lounge. Tell them who paid, Shawna said.
Tell them who missed, Tank said. He reached for another vase. It was
heavier than expected; he lifted it easily, then discovered it blocked
the entire doorway.

4
00:01:10,821 --> 00:01:34,318
Mercedes waited with her arms folded while he turned one way, then the
other. Nigga, turn the flowers. I am turning. You turning yourself.
The flowers ain't learned nothing. He finally got through sideways.
Rosa, passing him in the hall, plucked one blue rose from the top.
Thank you. That's from the duke. Then thank you for intercepting it.
We had moved suites.

5
00:01:34,568 --> 00:01:58,099
Shawna wanted curtains without bullet holes and a balcony she hadn't
watched men climb over. The hotel gave us the whole top floor. The
manager cried while handing over the keys, and my wife quietly made
him sit down and drink water before anybody asked him for anything
else. Tank returned empty-handed. Can I deplore his ass off the boat
tonight?

6
00:01:58,349 --> 00:02:18,672
Get dressed first, I said. Nigga, we got invited. The three attackers
were downstairs in the custody of Commandant Odette Valeur, a forty-
six-year-old woman with silver at her temples and a white uniform she
wore like an argument nobody had won yet. She commanded the harbor
police.

7
00:02:18,923 --> 00:02:40,195
She had come to arrest the men, looked at my badge, looked at the
broken suite and asked who had put the fountain man in the fountain.
Inez, I said. Odette nodded toward her. Good distance. Then she took
the prisoners somewhere Bellario couldn't collect them with a polite
note. I liked her immediately. Bellario denied everything.

8
00:02:40,445 --> 00:03:05,377
The duke announced that the attackers had been jealous gamblers acting
without permission. Nigga, without permission from who? He left that
part floating. Bellario vanished from the next day's press events, but
his feather appeared on an assistant's hat, and that was almost more
disrespectful. Odette visited us again the afternoon of the
masquerade. Lark spread Amalia's papers across the table.

9
00:03:05,627 --> 00:03:28,801
Cassius put his father's bird beside them. Luc told her about the
missing staff. She listened to every word. Then she looked at me. If I
take this to the palace alone, it disappears into a drawer. If you
show it to the whole harbor while winning his race, the drawer becomes
difficult to close. Nigga, I can make it a convertible. Her mouth
twitched.

10
00:03:29,051 --> 00:03:52,988
I've seen your driving. She gave us one useful fact: the Sovereign Sun
would leave the harbor after the masquerade and reach Cinder Dock the
next night. Its scheduled crew had been replaced. Some of the
replacements had not volunteered. Lark stood up. Mateo? Possibly. That
word is killing me. Odette held her gaze. I won't give you a better
one unless I have it.

11
00:03:53,238 --> 00:04:16,297
Lark sat down slowly. Mercedes put an arm around her shoulders without
making her look at anybody. That evening my people came down the hotel
staircase like the building had spent its entire life waiting for
them. Tank wore black velvet and a silver mask that covered half his
face. Rosa wore a red gown and a mask made of little dark feathers.

12
00:04:16,547 --> 00:04:40,867
Mercedes had chosen a white suit with nothing timid about it. Porsche
wore gold, from the heels to the tiny knife-shaped hairpin she
insisted was purely decorative and which I respectfully chose not to
investigate. Cassius wore a sling matched to his jacket. Inez had
traded her ankle wrap for a high boot and carried a cane topped with a
silver horse.

13
00:04:41,116 --> 00:05:04,732
She looked dangerous enough that several men on the staircase suddenly
remembered women could tell when they were staring. Shawna came last.
Black dress. Blue stones at her throat. A mask she took off before
reaching me because she wanted me to see her whole face when I forgot
how my lungs worked. Nigga, Tank said behind me. I know. Nigga, you
see your wife?

14
00:05:04,982 --> 00:05:27,515
I am actively seeing her. You look like you need a chair. Go find your
woman. Rosa took his hand. He found her. Shawna stopped on the step
above me and straightened my collar. Try to keep the tuxedo intact.
Depends how the tuxedo behaves. She kissed me. Somebody farther down
the staircase started applauding. Then the whole lobby joined in.

15
00:05:27,765 --> 00:05:50,864
Nigga, I couldn't even kiss my wife privately in a room full of
strangers anymore. Fame had become an audience with poor boundaries. I
bowed anyway. The Sovereign Sun waited beyond the harbor wall, longer
than a street, white and gold beneath a thousand lights. Its bow
opened into a ballroom. I am telling you exactly what I saw.

16
00:05:51,114 --> 00:06:13,482
The front of the boat had split into two great curved doors, revealing
a dance floor that seemed to float above the water. A staircase
descended toward the tenders, and musicians played from balconies
inside the ship's mouth. Tank stared up at it. This nigga boat got
teeth? Those are columns, Rosa said. That's how they get you.

17
00:06:13,732 --> 00:06:40,188
A steward in a white coat led us aboard. On the wall behind him hung
portraits of previous Grand Prix winners. I recognized Esteban in one,
younger, standing beside Nero and Amalia with a trophy between them.
Somebody had moved a large vase in front of Nero's face. Cassius
stopped. I moved the vase. The steward opened his mouth. Nigga, choose
your next words carefully.

18
00:06:40,438 --> 00:07:02,916
He shut it. We entered the ballroom together. There were dukes,
actresses, drivers, singers, women who charged rich men for the
pleasure of their company and rich men who believed nobody could tell.
Champagne moved through the room on silver trays. A pianist played a
song that made the women at our table look at one another and smile.

19
00:07:03,166 --> 00:07:25,383
Mercedes whispered something to Porsche, and both of them walked
toward a man in a white dinner jacket before he had time to flee. That
their friend? Tank asked. That look like a debt. The duke stood
beneath a chandelier shaped like a crown. Aiden, he said. You honor my
ship. Ship was overdue. His eyes moved over my people.

20
00:07:25,633 --> 00:07:51,800
Counted Cassius's sling, Inez's cane, Shawna's bare shoulders. Stopped
at Odette, who had come aboard separately in a black dress with her
badge at the waist. A commandant at a masquerade, he said. Odette
smiled. A duke hosting one. We all enjoy costumes. Nigga, I almost
proposed friendship on the spot. Aurelio turned to Shawna. I hope
tonight's entertainment meets your standards.

21
00:07:52,050 --> 00:08:14,314
My standards are sitting beside me. She took my arm. I looked at the
duke and smiled with every tooth God had trusted me with. He announced
the evening's exhibition after the first dance. Two cars waited on a
circular platform behind the ballroom: a silver roadster and a black
coupe with a blue interior. They belonged to the prize fleet.

22
00:08:14,564 --> 00:08:36,738
Guests could bid for the right to challenge the leading driver in a
short timed run along the ship's upper deck. Nigga had put a racetrack
on a yacht. I finally understood why rich people kept getting invited
places. Sometimes one of them had a good idea. The duke held up a
little gold key. The challenger wagers fifty thousand.

23
00:08:36,988 --> 00:09:01,970
If he defeats Captain Aiden, he keeps the roadster. If he loses? I
asked. The money supports the Grand Prix. The workers? The
institution. Nigga, the institution can get a job. My races pay the
workers. A murmur crossed the room. Aurelio watched the faces around
him and adjusted smoothly. Of course. Tonight's proceeds shall go to
the staff.

24
00:09:02,220 --> 00:09:24,078
Porsche, across the room, raised her phone so he could see it
recording. Say the amount too. He said it. Then Inez stepped forward.
I'll race. Cassius caught her elbow. Your ankle. It's my left ankle.
And still attached to the rest of you. She looked at him. He looked
back. Something quiet happened between them. Not soft exactly.

25
00:09:24,328 --> 00:09:50,412
Two people recognizing the same fear from opposite sides. She lowered
her hand. Fine. I'll choose his challenger. The duke laughed. And whom
do you choose? She pointed at him. The whole ballroom turned.
Aurelio's smile remained. Only his eyes moved. I do not usually—
Nigga, you own the competition, I reminded him. Drive something. The
applause began at our table. Spread outward.

26
00:09:50,662 --> 00:10:13,100
Became impossible to ignore without looking smaller than the portrait
behind him. He handed his glass to Bellario's assistant. All right, he
said. The duke's assistant tried to hand me a waiver. "Nigga, what's
this?" "Acknowledgment of the exhibition." "I acknowledge that nigga
challenged the room and the room pointed at him." Inez took the paper.

27
00:10:13,350 --> 00:10:36,438
"It says he's not responsible for disappointment." "Which nigga?" Tank
asked. "The duke." "That nigga responsible for half mine already."
Aurelio held out his hand for the page. "Shall we drive?" "Nigga," I
said, "I've been dressed for it since the harbor." Shawna kissed my
cheek. "Go. The nigga's gloves are getting nervous." We went up to the
deck.

28
00:10:36,688 --> 00:10:56,586
The track circled the yacht's upper level around two pools, a glass
conservatory and a helipad. The cars had been arranged for display,
but the road was real enough and wide enough to make a bad decision
feel generous. Floodlights shone over the water. Guests lined the
balconies below us.

29
00:10:56,836 --> 00:11:18,290
The captain's bridge glowed at the front of the ship, guarded by two
men in dark coats. I watched those men while the duke chose the silver
roadster. Lark had gone below with Luc to look for familiar crew.
Mercedes and Porsche followed a steward who had whispered to them at
the bar. Shawna stayed at the railing with Rosa and Odette.

30
00:11:18,540 --> 00:11:41,357
Nobody needed to be taken away from me to have something to do. My
people were already moving. Aurelio pulled on leather gloves. Do you
know what the difference is between a guest and an owner? he asked.
Guest can leave without selling the furniture. An owner decides when
the evening ends. Nigga, we'll see. We started together. He was good.

31
00:11:41,607 --> 00:12:00,682
That surprised me for half a second. Then it pleased me. I wanted the
man to have at least one real thing to lose. His roadster took the
first curve cleanly. I stayed close in the black coupe. We swept
around the glass conservatory with the sea falling away beyond the
rail.

32
00:12:00,932 --> 00:12:23,257
He accelerated toward the helipad, then moved across my line hard
enough to make his intention plain. This wasn't a polite exhibition.
Good. I came around the outside. He tried to shut the gap. I let him
think he had, then took the next turn so close to the pool that water
rose over my left wheels. The guests below screamed.

33
00:12:23,507 --> 00:12:45,767
On the far balcony, Tank was jumping up and down in his velvet suit
like a furious wedding cake. Nigga, get him! I got him. At the final
bend I moved alongside the duke, looked straight across into his car
and smiled. He saw it. Lost one fraction of a second deciding whether
to hate me or the smile. I used the fraction.

34
00:12:46,017 --> 00:13:08,095
The black coupe crossed the line first. I stopped at the railing. The
ballroom below erupted. Aurelio rolled to a halt beside me, both hands
still on the wheel. For the first time all night he looked his age. I
got out and held up the car's key. For the staff, I said. The cheering
doubled. Then a gunshot came from below deck.

35
00:13:08,345 --> 00:13:26,520
The cheering stopped so abruptly I could hear the ocean against the
hull. Shawna was already moving toward the stairway. I jumped the low
rail, landed on the lower platform and reached her at the door. Rosa
and Odette were behind her. Tank thundered down from the other side.

36
00:13:26,770 --> 00:13:52,392
Lark came out of a corridor carrying a man whose white shirt was
stained at the shoulder. Luc held his other arm. Mercedes followed
with three women in crew uniforms. Porsche came last, face hard, a
broken champagne bottle in her hand. Somebody asked the wrong
question, she said. Behind them, two guards rounded the corner. Odette
showed her badge. Stop. One lifted his gun.

37
00:13:52,642 --> 00:14:16,555
I hit him with the door. Nigga, it was a beautiful door. Heavy wood,
brass edge. Somebody had paid excellent money for it to become part of
his problem. His weapon struck the floor. Tank caught the second man
against the corridor wall and made the wall reconsider its career.
Shawna took the wounded crewman's weight from Lark. Where's Mateo?
Lark asked him.

38
00:14:16,805 --> 00:14:42,648
The man shook his head, breath catching. Island. They moved him ahead.
She went pale. Alive? He nodded. Yes. For a second she couldn't stand.
Mercedes caught her around the waist. Nigga alive, she said firmly.
Hear that part first. The wounded man looked at Cassius, who had
reached us with Inez. Chrome? Cassius froze. Yes. The man's eyes
filled. Your father said you'd come.

39
00:14:42,898 --> 00:15:05,765
Cassius made a sound I had never heard from him, not when his car hung
over the cliff, not when we read the letter. It was smaller than a
word and much harder to hear. Aurelio appeared at the top of the
stairs. Captain, this has become disorderly. I turned toward him.
Nigga, I haven't started. Below us, the yacht's great bow doors began
closing.

40
00:15:06,015 --> 00:15:29,319
The ballroom narrowed around the sea. He was ending the evening. I
looked at the black coupe above us, then at the open front of the
ship, then at the harbor launch approaching beyond it with blue lights
flashing. Odette followed my eyes. No, she said. Yes, I said. You
cannot drive a car through the ballroom. Nigga, watch the piano. Tank
started laughing.

41
00:15:29,569 --> 00:15:33,589
That was all the encouragement a man like me required.
